Subject: [PATCH] build: declare zstd for the kernel and kunit on the Debian rung
Origin: other, Peios catalogue qualification review
Upstream-Status: Pending [Debian reference dependency list]

build.kernel and build.kunit ask for com.facebook.zstd on the native rung but
not for zstd on the Debian one. The config enables CONFIG_KERNEL_ZSTD and
CONFIG_MODULE_COMPRESS_ZSTD, so the Debian build compiled the whole kernel and
then stopped making the compressed image:

    /bin/sh: 1: zstd: not found
    make[3]: *** [arch/x86/boot/compressed/Makefile:151:
      arch/x86/boot/compressed/vmlinux.bin.zst] Error 127

The omission was invisible until now because the Debian rung never reached
this point: it had previously failed at build:upstream, and then at the rustc
gate. build.fwsig and test.fwsig already declare zstd on both rungs.

It is the only gap between the two lists for these targets; bash and gzip are
Essential in Debian.

diff --git a/pekit.toml b/pekit.toml
index 57fad71..7273cc7 100644
--- a/pekit.toml
+++ b/pekit.toml
@@ -162,6 +162,7 @@ python3 = "*"
 perl = "*"
 tar = "*"
 xz-utils = "*"
+zstd = "*"
 
 [build.kernel]
 keyring_inputs = ["modsig.pub", "tcb.pub"]
@@ -253,6 +254,7 @@ python3 = "*"
 perl = "*"
 tar = "*"
 xz-utils = "*"
+zstd = "*"
 
 # Export the sanitized userspace UAPI headers (full Linux UAPI + our pkm/*.h,
 # which ride along since they're staged under include/uapi/pkm). Depends on
